      "raw_html": "<div class=\"question\" id=\"question-213293\"><div class=\"questionHeader\"><span class=\"questionNumber\">18.</span><span class=\"helpButton\" questionid=\"213293\">?</span></div><div class=\"questionText\"><p>Christmas in 2100 will be celebrated, as usual, on December 25th. Given that January 1st, 2100, is a Friday, use congruences to determine the day of the week on which Christmas will be celebrated in 2100.</p>\n<p><em>Hint: The year 2100 is not a leap year since it's an end-of-century year (multiple of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"270\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\"><mjx-math aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml display=\"inline\" unselectable=\"on\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>) and is not divisible by <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"271\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\"><mjx-math aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c34\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2E\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml display=\"inline\" unselectable=\"on\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>400.</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></em></p>\n</div><div class=\"answerDetails\"><div class=\"questionDifficulty difficultyEasy\">E</div><span class=\"answerCreated\">Sun, Oct 11th @ 3:59 AM</span><span class=\"answerDetailsSeparator\">|</span><span class=\"timeElpased\">Elapsed: 0:13</span><span class=\"answerResult\"><span style=\"color: green;\">Correct</span></span></div></div>"
